Z||000002||ChadMan||08-30-99||07:10 AM||||Supposedly, the quickest Fiero in the 1/4 miles is the V-6 4-speed. (Note I didn't say "slickest-shifting" or "comfortable highway cruiser" or "highest top speed"...if these were true I wouldn't wish for a 5-speed.)  It would stand to reason that a 4-speed V6 85 SE without weight-adding power accessories would be the quickest stock Fiero.<p>Car and Driver tested an SD(Super Duty)-4 Fiero (the article is in Brooklands' Fiero book).  It was a tuned-down version of the race motor they used for IMSA GTU competition.  It made about 180 hp and ran 0-60 in something like 6.5 sec, if memory serves.  It was a cool-looking car, too, with DGP flared bodywork and 16" Centerline wheels.
Z||000003||DXR_WILL||08-30-99||06:25 PM||||I came across the same site today at work (http://members.aol.com/topfiero/index.htm). I thought the 5 speed V6's were a little bite faster then the 4 speeds.  This site has some really cool articles.  I realy like the one about the Fiero VS. Dodge's Stealth Twin Turbo. 
Z||000004||88 Fiero||08-31-99||01:28 PM||||Hello to everyone...the SD4 stands for Super Duty 4 Cyclinder. This is the engine the Pontiac used to dominate IMSA and GTU race. Back in the 80's you can buy this SD 4 engine package. There was one guy in east coast that have a SD4 in his fiero. It was punch out to 2.7 liters and producing 275 horses and very wicked to all the V8 cars. The 4 speed tranny can be vicious and eat up the Getrag 5 speed. My friend Keith of Fiero Motorsports have the 4 speed on his fiero but change the final gear ratio to 4.10...mann talk about bad M#%$*@F---!!! But believe me it will beat the 5 speed getrag...<br>}:-}
